==English==
{{wikipedia|River Thames}}
{{wikipedia|Thames, New Zealand}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Temese}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Temes}}, {{m|ang|Temese}} (cognate with {{cog|cy|Tafwys}}), from {{der|en|la|Tamesis}}, {{m|la|Tamesas}}<ref>{{R:ine:EIEC|147}}</ref>, possibly from {{der|en|cel-pro|*tamesās||river, waters|lit=darkness}}, masculine ā-stem of {{m|cel-pro|*tames}}<ref>{{R:cel:Matasovic_2009|378}}</ref>, s-stem of {{der|en|ine-pro|*tm̥Hes-}}, zero-grade of {{m|ine-pro|*témHes-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*témHos-||darkness}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*temH-||dark}}. Related to {{der|en|cel-pro|*temeslos||darkness}}, {{m|cel-pro|*temos||dark}}.

A parallel in Proto-Celtic of "dark, darkness" taking on the figurative meaning of "water" can also be found in {{cog|cel-pro|*dubros||water, dark}}, from {{cog|ine-pro|*dʰubrós||dark}}, yielding {{cog|cy|dŵr||water}}, {{cog|ga|dobhar||water, sea, dark, gloomy}}.

Alternatively from {{der|en|cel-pro|*tā-}}<ref>{{cite-journal|1996|Kitson, Peter R.|British and European River Names|Transactions of the Philological Society|volume=94|issue=2|doi=10.1111/j.1467-968X.1996.tb01178.x|pages=73–118}}</ref>, {{m|cel-pro|*tāyo-||to melt, flow}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*teh₂-||to melt}}, or from unknown non-Indo-European root<ref>{{cite-book|1955|Jackson, Kenneth H.|The Pictish Language|chapter=The Problem of the Picts|editors=Wainright, F. T.|location=Edinburgh|publisher=Nelson|pages=129–166}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|1998|Coates, Richard|A new explanation of the name of London|Transactions of the Philological Society|volume=96|issue=2|url=http://www.blackwell-synergy.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/1467-968X.00027|doi=10.1111/1467-968X.00027|pages=203–229}}</ref>.

Possible cognates include the names of rivers and tributaries such as:
* [[Tamar]] (from {{cog|la|Tamarus}})<ref name="Falileyev" /><ref>{{cite-book|2012|Delamarre, Xavier|Noms de lieux celtiques de l'Europe ancienne (-500 / +500): dictionnaire|publisher=Errance|location=Arles|isbn=978-2-87772-483-8}}</ref>, [[Tavy]], [[Teifi]] (from {{cog|cy|Teifi}}, from {{cog|owl|Tebi}}, {{m|owl|Teibi}}), [[Teme]], and [[Teviot]] ({{cog|la|Tefius}}, {{m|la|Teifius}}) in Great Britain
* [[Tambre]] (from {{cog|la|Tamaris}})<ref name="Falileyev">{{cite-book|2010|Falileyev, Alexander|Dictionary of Continental Celtic Place-names: A Celtic Companion to the Barrington Atlas of the Greek and Roman World|publisher=CMCS Publications|isbn=978-0955718236}}</ref>, [[Támega]] (in Galician, {{cog|pt|Tâmega}}, {{cog|la|Tamice}}), [[Támoga]] or [[Támboga]] ({{cog|la|Tamega}}), and [[Tamuxe]], all of them flowing through Galicia (Spain) and northern Portugal
* [[Tamaran]] in France
* [[Tammaro]] (from {{cog|la|Tamarus}}) in Italy
* [[Demer]] in Belgium
* [[Tamyras]] in [[Phoenicia]]

